Drop .conf files here to override HAF's PostgreSQL settings. The directory is
bind-mounted into the HAF container and read after its shipped configuration,
so anything set here wins.

HAF ships shared_buffers at 16 GiB, tuned for full Hive. On a Pixagram node the
database is a fraction of that, and Postgres will refuse to start if it cannot
reserve the memory. Below roughly 24 GB of RAM, create local.conf here:

  shared_buffers = 2GB
  effective_cache_size = 4GB
  maintenance_work_mem = 512MB
